## Summary Table

| # | Gap | Severity | Blocks Runtime? |
|---|-----|----------|-----------------|
| 1 | Missing historical data in claim_context | CRITICAL | No (defaults to 0, but Layer 2 is silently useless) |
| 2 | Circular import risk in __init__.py | LOW | No (works now, fragile) |
| 3 | Name collision: two FraudAssessmentResponse | MEDIUM | No (causes confusion) |
| 4 | Missing __init__.py files | CRITICAL | Yes (if missing, imports fail) |
| 5 | Hardcoded 0.7 threshold | MEDIUM | No (behavioral inconsistency) |
| 6 | Duplicate Layer 2 calls in wrappers | LOW | No (performance only) |
| 7 | API returns dict instead of 404 | HIGH | Yes (500 error on missing assessment) |
| 8 | behavioral_flags not persisted to DB | MEDIUM | No (data loss on read-back) |
| 9 | External AI stub raises NotImplementedError | LOW | No (caught by fallback) |
